! C22-6578 PROBLEM 1.5, METHOD 1, "Use chain indexing", printed p.8
! (PDF 9), read in the ink, EXACTLY AS PRINTED including the PRNID,
! PUNID, SLC and END that comment (a) says "should be included in every
! program intended for assembly."
!
!   "Replace the following full words by zeros: DOG through DOG + 24.0,
!   CAT through CAT + 15.0.  CHICK through CHICK + 34.0"
!
! The page does not place DOG, CAT and CHICK; the data below does, and
! adding it is the only change.  Comment (b): "a simple demonstration
! of the utility of the automatic refill feature".
!
! WHY "CB, $1, $-1.0" RETURNS TO THE Z: Z, CBR+ and CB are half words
! and the Z is on a word boundary: $-1.0 from the CB is the Z.
! Reference Manual printed p.27, CBR "is identical to COUNT AND BRANCH,
! except that in addition the index word specified by J is refilled if
! the count reached zero."  LINK 3's refill is "$", itself.
!
! Final state: $2 refilled from LINK 3 = CHICK, 35, LINK 3; $1 count 0.
!
! THE PAGE PRINTS "LINK 1" WITH A BLANK.  C22-6531 printed p.8: "Blanks
! have no meaning in any field except to indicate the spacing desired
! on the printed output listing."  Written here closed up, as every MCP
! deck writes its V RCW-style symbols.

        PRNID, JOE BLOWE, DEPT. 333
        PUNID, J. BLOWE
        SLC, 1000.0
        LCI, $1, 3.0
        LX, $2, LINK1
        Z, 0($2)
        CBR+, $2, $-0.32
        CB, $1, $-1.0
HALT    BEW, $
LINK1   XW, DOG, 25, LINK2
LINK2   XW, CAT, 16, LINK3
LINK3   XW, CHICK, 35, $

! DOG, CAT, CHICK: a guard either side of each, all sevens.
        SLC, 1200.0
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
DOG     DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        SLC, 1230.0
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
CAT     DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
